            <ArticleTitle>Fentiazac as an oral analgesic for postoperative dental pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>787-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The analgesic activity of a single 200-mg dose of fentiazac was examined in 60 patients who had undergone 12 types of oral surgery. Patients completed a questionnaire that subjectively classified pain intensity and pain relief from 30 minutes to eight hours after they took the drug. General response to fentiazac was excellent, and no adverse effects were reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
